WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.609 --> 00:00:05.049
In Season 1, Episode 6 of "The Big Bang Theory,"
"The Middle Earth Paradigm," Penny throws

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:06.860
a Halloween party in her apartment.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.469
Leonard shows up as a Hobbit, hoping to show
Penny he can fit into her circle of friends.

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:16.000
But things take a disappointing turn when
Penny's beefy ex-boyfriend Kurt shows up,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.410
decked out in a physique-baring fur loincloth.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.740
And when Leonard manages to insult Kurt's
marginal intelligence, the angered muscleman

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.050
hoists Leonard off his hairy Hobbit feet.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.949
As Johnny Galecki says in author Jessica Radloff's
"The Big Bang Theory: The Definitive, Inside

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:35.740
Story of the Epic Hit Series," the scene took
him back to his youth.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.597
He admitted,

00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:40.450
"Him picking me up as Leonard really affected
me to the point where I think I cried after

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.160
we shot the episode […] it really dug up
some old schoolyard stuff for me.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.320
I had a way into Leonard and really began
to understand him."

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:51.541
So while the scene may have been intense for
the actor, it also opened a window into the

00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:56.793
character Galecki would play for over 270
more episodes of "The Big Bang Theory."

